# EAS cloud-build upload filter for the Aquatrack app (mobile/).
# This repository also holds the web CRM and the backend; none of that is needed to build the Android app.
# NOTE: when this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so the secret / dependency rules are repeated here.

# Everything at the repo root except the mobile app
/*
!/mobile

# Inside mobile/: dependencies are installed fresh in the cloud (npm ci from package-lock.json)
/mobile/node_modules
# Generated native project and local build outputs (EAS prebuilds its own)
/mobile/android
/mobile/ios
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/dist
/mobile/web-build
/mobile/*.log
/mobile/*.apk
/mobile/*.aab

# Local npm override that would hide peer-dependency conflicts (what broke the first cloud build): install strictly
/mobile/.npmrc

# Secrets and local environment: never uploaded. API address etc. come from the EAS environment (eas env:*)
/mobile/.env
/mobile/.env.*
!/mobile/.env.example
/mobile/*.jks
/mobile/*.keystore
/mobile/*.p12
/mobile/*.pem
/mobile/google-services.json
/mobile/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
